.SH "RETURN VALUE"
These functions return
.B ERR
upon failure and
.B OK
upon success.
.PP
In
.IR \%ncurses ","
they return
.B ERR
if
.bP
the
.I curses
screen has not been initialized,
.bP
(for functions taking a
.I \%WINDOW
pointer argument)
.I win
is a null pointer,
or
.bP
scrolling is not enabled in the window
(as by \fB\%scrollok\fP(3X)).
